    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d103">

                <pb facs="0406" n="371" xml:id="pg371"/>

                <head>103. Memorandum From the Special Assistant to the President’s Assistant for
                    National Security Affairs (Inderfurth)
                    to the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs (Brzezinski)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d103-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1978-10-24">October 24, 1978</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>[<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>]</item>
                </list>
                <p>We received the attached CIA proposal<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d103-f2"/> on Monday.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d103-f3"/> It was
                    staffed to Henze who has distributed it
                    to SCC principals. Stan Turner may want to discuss this on Wednesday,<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d103-f4"/> hence I am providing it to you for your information.</p>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">7½ lines not declassified</hi>]</p>
                <p>I suggest, by the way, that if this assistance is to be provided, it should be
                    done <hi rendition="#italic">quickly.</hi> Months of delay, [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">less than 1 line not declassified</hi>] could prove
                    harmful. [<hi rendition="#italic">2½ lines not declassified</hi>] My hunch is
                    that there isn’t, but we should explore this.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d103-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d103-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Security Council, Carter
                    Administration Intelligence Files, Box I–025, Egypt 3 Feb. 1977–16 Aug. 1979.
                    Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d103-f2" n="2" xml:id="d103-f2-content">
                <p>Attached but not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d103-f3" n="3" xml:id="d103-f3-content">
                <p>October 23.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d103-f4" n="4" xml:id="d103-f4-content">
                <p>October 25.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
